      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#Process",
      "name": "Publish an ArchiMate model — every picture derived from it",
      "summary": "An ArchiMate model is authored in Archi and committed; everything a reader sees is derived from it by three mechanical Tools, in order, in the pipeline lane: `archimate-check` (it parses and resolves), `archimate-metamodel` (the element types and relationship…",
      "description": "An ArchiMate model is authored in Archi and committed; everything a reader sees is derived from it by three mechanical Tools, in order, in the pipeline lane: `archimate-check` (it parses and resolves), `archimate-metamodel` (the element types and relationship patterns it uses, each checked against ArchiMate's relationship table), and `archimate-pages` (a page and an IRI for every view, element and relationship, every view drawn, and the \"Metamodel in use\" page). No step draws a diagram by hand, and none runs Archi or a JVM (skill `archimate-models`).\n\nOwner, 2026-10-31: \"i dont really like native UML, rather derived\", then \"make mechanical tools as parts of skills/processes\". A metamodel used to be a hand-drawn view of placeholder elements named after their types; here it is the second step's output, so it cannot disagree with the model.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "sourcePath": "processes/ui/archimate-publish.bpmn",
